# The partner repositories molpy is built against. scripts/partners.py
# resolves them, for every workflow (`partners.py fetch`) and for the git
# hooks (`partners.py run`) alike, so a local push is tested against the same
# molrs commit as CI -- never against whatever the sibling ../molrs happens to
# have checked out.
#
# KEY=VALUE lines only. SELF is this repository's directory in CI's sibling
# layout (molpy/, molrs/).
#
# On dev, partners are tracked, not pinned: MOLRS_REF=dev is molrs's dev tip
# -- or molrs's branch of the same name as the one being built, when molrs has
# one (a change spanning both repositories; see "Partners" in
# docs/developer/development-setup.md). pyproject.toml builds molcrafts-molrs
# from that checkout ([tool.uv.sources]). A release is tested against molrs
# from PyPI instead (docs/developer/release-process.md).
#
# uv.lock records molrs's package metadata (its version and dependencies), not
# a commit. When molrs's dev changes that metadata, `uv lock --check` fails;
# relock in a commit of its own:
#   scripts/partners.py run -- sh -c 'uv lock && cp uv.lock "$PARTNERS_SOURCE/"'
SELF=molpy
MOLRS_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/molrs
MOLRS_REF=dev
